## Strings of desktop/notification-settings (Settings > Notifications; read off the live client 2026-10-15)
notifications-settings-overview = Overview
notifications-settings-desktop = Enable Desktop Notifications
notifications-settings-desktop-description = If you’re looking for per-channel or per-server notifications, right-click the desired server icon and select Notification Settings.
notifications-settings-taskbar = Enable Taskbar Flashing
notifications-settings-taskbar-description = Flashes the app in your taskbar when you have new notifications.
notifications-settings-notify-me = Notify me when...
notifications-settings-go-live = People I know start streaming in small servers
notifications-settings-anniversary = A friend and I reach a friendship anniversary
notifications-settings-friends-online = Friends come online
notifications-settings-profile-updates = Friends update their profile
notifications-settings-reactions = Someone reacts to my messages
notifications-settings-reactions-all = All Messages
notifications-settings-reactions-dms = Only Direct Messages
notifications-settings-never = Never
notifications-settings-sounds = Sounds
notifications-settings-new-message = New Message
notifications-settings-selected-channel = New Message in the channel I’m currently reading
notifications-settings-incoming-ring = Incoming Ring
notifications-settings-disable-all = Disable All Notification Sounds
notifications-settings-disable-all-description = Disables all notification sounds, including voice and video sound effects. Your individual sound preferences will be saved and restored if you turn this on.
notifications-settings-voice-sounds-description = Enable/disable sounds that play when you’re in a call, like Mute, Unmute, Deafen and more.
notifications-settings-badges = Badges
notifications-settings-badge = Enable Unread Message Badge
notifications-settings-badge-description = Shows a red badge on the app icon when you have unread messages.
notifications-settings-advanced = Advanced
notifications-settings-advanced-show = Show Advanced Notification Settings
notifications-settings-advanced-hide = Hide Advanced Notification Settings
notifications-settings-mobile-delay = Mobile Notification Delay
notifications-settings-mobile-delay-description = Discord won’t send push notifications to your mobile device while you’re active on your computer. Use this setting to choose how long you need to be inactive on desktop before mobile notifications start again.
notifications-settings-minutes = { $minutes ->
    [one] { $minutes } minute
   *[other] { $minutes } minutes
}
notifications-settings-tts-command = Allow playback and usage of /tts command
notifications-settings-tts-command-description = Using the /tts command speaks your message out loud. Turn this off if you prefer to see /tts messages as text only. You can control the speed of playback on the [Accessibility]({ $onClick }) page.
notifications-settings-tts-messages = Speak all messages out loud
notifications-settings-tts-messages-description = Speaks messages out loud, even if they weren’t using the /tts command.
notifications-settings-tts-all = For all channels
notifications-settings-tts-selected = Only for currently selected channel
